{"availability":"available","full":"vibgrate/cli","name":"cli","description":"Local codebase intelligence for AI coding agents and software teams, in the CLI and VS Code. Vibgrate builds a deterministic Code Graph, measures dependency and runtime drift with DriftScore, maps architecture and blast radius, analyses dependency and vulnerability risk, and generates SBOM/VEX.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":5,"forks":6,"created":"2026-02-27T09:53:37Z","updated":"2026-10-11T06:57:40Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://vibgrate.com","topics":["ai-assisted","ai-coding-agent","ai-coding-assistant","archtecture","cli","code-graph","codebase-analysis","codebase-intelligence","dependency-graph","dependency-management","drift-score","drift-scorecards","mcp","nodejs","sbom","security","software-modernization","typescript","upgrade-drift"],"demo":"https://vibgrate.com/cli","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.411Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.411Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.411Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.411Z","stars":5,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Local codebase intelligence for AI coding agents — graph, drift, and version-correct docs on your machine","Everything runs on your machine. No API key, no network call, no data leaving your repo unless you explicitly push. The vibgrate command is an alias for vg — they are interchangeable.","Trade-off: no model ships with the CLI, and VG Code is only as good as the model you point it at. A 7B local model is not a frontier model — it buys you privacy, offline inference, and no per-token cost. Relay buys you capacity at a per-token price. Pick the tier that matches the task; the graph grounding is the same either way."],"features":["What is this codebase? — A deterministic code graph: call trees, import paths, impact surfaces, dependency facts.","How far behind is it? — A ranked DriftScore (0–100) with runtime/framework lag, dependency age and EOL proximity, and a prioritized fix list. Exposure is scored separately as a RiskScore; the two together are the…","Can we fix it here? — VG Code, a coding agent whose search tool is the code graph, not a grep — in your terminal as vg code and as the VG Code panel in Vibgrate for VS Code — plus vg fix, ranked upgrade plans it can…","Search is the graph. searchcode resolves symbols, callers, and callees from the map vg build produced — so the model gets the three functions that matter, not forty files that mention the word.","Blast radius before the edit. graphimpact tells the model what depends on a symbol before it changes it, and vg tests knows which tests to run after."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0d47c67122b1356ac39a6dc6b8b8bc0c0571596fa61157e4a68921daf8adcf6f","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.470Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.470Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Local codebase intelligence for AI coding agents — graph, drift, and version-correct docs on your machine","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"vg serve starts Vibgrate AI Context — a local-first MCP server that gives any MCP-compatible assistant (Claude, Cursor, Windsurf, Copilot, Gemini CLI, …) your code map, offline drift, local models, and version-correct library docs, all from your machine (no account, nothing uploaded; thin local docs fall through to the hosted catalog unless you pass --local).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"With a pulled model there is no account and no key, and Code Modes fit the model to the machine.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"When a task needs more, Vibgrate Relay supplies hosted models on your Vibgrate account — no per-provider API keys — and falls back to your local model if it is unreachable.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"VG Code additionally needs a model: a local runtime (a Code Mode pack, Ollama, LM Studio, or a GGUF on disk), a Vibgrate Relay token, or an API key for another hosted provider.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"0d47c67122b1356ac39a6dc6b8b8bc0c0571596fa61157e4a68921daf8adcf6f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.472Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T06:57:40Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vibgrate/cli/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:27:04.475Z","hash":"0d47c67122b1356ac39a6dc6b8b8bc0c0571596fa61157e4a68921daf8adcf6f","originalBytes":67069,"storedBytes":67069,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["vibgrate","code","local","scan","what","model","build","evidence","graph","map","drift","one","serve","command","install","when","every","file","does","cli","path","review","same","bash","run","offline","agent","docs","json","change","runs","which","docs.md","hosted","never","files","impact","verify","models","push","sbom","already","any","key","machine","version","writes","before","compress","hcs","library","mcp","only","read","search","tool","against","assistant","context","export","cloud","config","list","tests","token","upgrade","vulnerabilities","advisory","ask","call","cyclonedx","default","deterministic","each","findings","format","gate","missing","mode","nothing","relay","report","sarif","score","session","step","attest","baseline","bundle","claude","compression","dependency","edit","exposure","full","how","memory","node","see","spdx","version-correct","back","commit","manifest","out","package","savings"